# Normalize all text files to LF in the repository regardless of the platform or editor that
# committed or checked them out. Without this, GitHub Actions' Windows runners (whose default
# git install has core.autocrlf=true) and its Linux/macOS runners (which do not convert line
# endings on checkout) produce different working-tree bytes from the same LF-stored blobs,
# which broke both `biome format --check` (hardcoded to `lf`) and the host-renderer's
# self-render idempotence check on a completely fresh clone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be subject to line-ending normalization.
*.png binary
*.zip binary
*.ico binary
